@@section 1
@@title SQ-NSM Namespace moves for the other jars, 2026-11-10 ([namespace_move.md](../namespace_move.md) section 5, TODO `creativesplit/ids #25`)
@@date 2026-11-10
@@jars creativebrewing creativecommon creativedelight creativedevtools creativeengineering creativemagic
@@sources feature_writeup/namespace_move.md
@@text
@@text Fixture (NSM fixture): a save built on the jars in `mods/` before the move, kept untouched; every row boots its own copy on the new jars (Common, Equipment, Magic, Compat, Delight, Brewing, Labels, Exposure, Worldgen, Calendar, Devtools). Content: a chest with one of each moved item (7 tier shields, 16 stepstools, 4 echo tools, air brake, felsic scrap, arrow fletching, flint and terrasteel, weathered cardboard box, netherite lunchbox with food inside), a tier shield and a stepstool worn (offhand, Curios feet), the same items dropped on the ground, a placed Dark Fire and a placed Weathered Cardboard Box, a Botanist Pot with a plant (Beautify), a Supplementaries jar holding a fluid, a Handcrafted nightstand holding items, two placed Immersive Paintings (one vanilla, one modded), a banner with a modded pattern, food seasoned with each of the 5 seasonings, notes and camera bags per SQ-NSM-09 and -10. Forceload the area and `/save-all flush` before stopping.
@@text
@@table
## SQ-NSM-01 | seasonings after the move (static half; crafting, overlay, eat bonus and JEI page are client)
@group Old save (NSM fixture) and new world
@commands Fixture copy: hover and eat a seasoned food from the old save. New world: season a food with each of the 5 seasonings (crafting), hover, eat; JEI Seasoning page
@pass Old stack: loads with no error or log spam, no seasoning lines (accepted loss). New: tooltip lines, the overlay on the icon, the eat bonus and the JEI page all work; `/data get entity @s SelectedItem` shows `creativedelight:<seasoning>` in `Seasonings`
@fails No overlay: `assets/creativedelight/models/item/seasoned/` missing from the Delight jar. No tag match: `#creativedelight:seasonable/<path>` not built (`seasoning_tags.js` reads the id)
@from batches/r1113/c4_a.qb
> zq bytype creativedelight:seasoning
> zq itemtag creativedelight:seasonable/pepper
> zq itemtag creativedelight:seasonable/chili
> zq itemtag creativedelight:seasonable/cheese
waitlog \[zq\] itemtag creativedelight:seasonable/cheese 30
count bytype creativedelight:seasoning >= 1
expect itemtag creativedelight:seasonable/pepper \([1-9]
expect itemtag creativedelight:seasonable/chili \([1-9]
expect itemtag creativedelight:seasonable/cheese \([1-9]
reject seasonable.*creativeengineering:

